I'm back from Beijing since late August. In Berkeley now. Lately, I've mainly
been thinking about AI safety and societal resilience. Of course, I have still
been studying lots of math; most recently computability and formal logic. Pure
mathematics is looking more and more like a purely recreational activity
lately, however. I still code for fun too!

I traveled a lot during the summer and I've generally been trying to do a
little less work and enjoy life more.

To that effect, the #link("/photos/gallery")[photo page] is now live, after a
long time procrastinating on it.

